{"track":"tahsili","num":"8.01","slug":"exponentials-logarithms","title":"Exponentials & Logarithms","subtitle":"ClipSAT Printable Practice Suite (clipsat.org) • Topic 8.01 • 20 FRQs + 25 MCQs • Difficulty Progression • Cross-Lesson Synthesis","sections":[{"heading":"Part I — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Foundational Fluency (1–7)","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $2^5$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating exponential expressions","answer":"$2^5=32$.","explanation":"$2^5=32$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","range":[-5,7],"points":[{"x":-2,"label":"P"},{"x":4,"label":"Q"}]}},{"q":"Evaluate $3^{-2}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating exponential expressions","answer":"$3^{-2}=\\frac{1}{9}$.","explanation":"$3^{-2}=\\frac{1}{9}$."},{"q":"Evaluate $16^{1/2}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating exponential expressions","answer":"$16^{1/2}=4$.","explanation":"$16^{1/2}=4$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_2 32$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating logarithms","answer":"Since $2^5=32$, $\\log_2 32=5$.","explanation":"Since $2^5=32$, $\\log_2 32=5$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_{10} 0.01$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Evaluating logarithms","answer":"Since $10^{-2}=0.01$, $\\log_{10}0.01=-2$.","explanation":"Since $10^{-2}=0.01$, $\\log_{10}0.01=-2$."},{"q":"Write $\\log_2(8x)$ as a sum of logarithms.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: product and quotient","answer":"$\\log_2(8x)=\\log_2 8+\\log_2 x=3+\\log_2 x$.","explanation":"$\\log_2(8x)=\\log_2 8+\\log_2 x=3+\\log_2 x$."},{"q":"Write $\\log_3\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)$ as a difference of logarithms.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: product and quotient","answer":"$\\log_3\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)=\\log_3 x-\\log_3 9=\\log_3 x-2$.","explanation":"$\\log_3\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)=\\log_3 x-\\log_3 9=\\log_3 x-2$."}]},{"heading":"Part II — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Intermediate Multi-Step Application (8–14)","questions":[{"q":"Combine $\\log_5 5+\\log_5 25$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: product and quotient","answer":"$\\log_5(5\\times25)=\\log_5 125=3$ (since $5^3=125$).","explanation":"$\\log_5(5\\times25)=\\log_5 125=3$ (since $5^3=125$)."},{"q":"Combine $\\log_2 24-\\log_2 3$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: product and quotient","answer":"$\\log_2\\left(\\frac{24}{3}\\right)=\\log_2 8=3$.","explanation":"$\\log_2\\left(\\frac{24}{3}\\right)=\\log_2 8=3$."},{"q":"Write $\\log(x^5)$ using the power rule.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: the power rule","answer":"$\\log(x^5)=5\\log x$.","explanation":"$\\log(x^5)=5\\log x$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_2(4^3)$ using the power rule.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: the power rule","answer":"$\\log_2(4^3)=3\\log_2 4=3(2)=6$.","explanation":"$\\log_2(4^3)=3\\log_2 4=3(2)=6$."},{"q":"Write $2\\log_3 x+\\log_3 y$ as a single logarithm.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Log laws: the power rule","answer":"$2\\log_3 x+\\log_3 y=\\log_3(x^2y)$.","explanation":"$2\\log_3 x+\\log_3 y=\\log_3(x^2y)$."},{"q":"Expand $\\log\\left(\\frac{x^3y}{z^2}\\right)$ fully.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions","answer":"$3\\log x+\\log y-2\\log z$.","explanation":"$3\\log x+\\log y-2\\log z$."},{"q":"Condense $3\\ln x-2\\ln y$ into a single logarithm.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions","answer":"$\\ln\\left(\\frac{x^3}{y^2}\\right)$.","explanation":"$\\ln\\left(\\frac{x^3}{y^2}\\right)$."}]},{"heading":"Part III — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (15–20)","questions":[{"q":"Expand $\\log_2\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^3\\right)$ fully.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions","cross_lesson":"6.01 Limits & Derivatives","answer":"$\\sqrt{x}=x^{1/2}$, so the expression equals $\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+3\\log_2 y$.","explanation":"$\\sqrt{x}=x^{1/2}$, so the expression equals $\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+3\\log_2 y$."},{"q":"Solve $2^x=32$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","cross_lesson":"7.01 Integration & Applications","answer":"$32=2^5$, so $x=5$.","explanation":"$32=2^5$, so $x=5$.","figure":{"type":"fn","title":"Logarithmic Curve & Domain (x > 0)","xrange":[-1,7],"yrange":[-3,4],"fns":[{"fn":"Math.log(x)","color":"var(--fig-indigo)","label":"y = ln(x)"}]}},{"q":"Solve $3^{x+1}=81$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","cross_lesson":"9.01 Statistics & Probability","answer":"$81=3^4$, so $x+1=4\\Rightarrow x=3$.","explanation":"$81=3^4$, so $x+1=4\\Rightarrow x=3$."},{"q":"Solve $5^{2x}=125$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","cross_lesson":"1.01 Algebra & Equations","answer":"$125=5^3$, so $2x=3\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3}{2}$.","explanation":"$125=5^3$, so $2x=3\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{3}{2}$."},{"q":"Solve $2^x=10$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving exponential equations using logarithms","cross_lesson":"2.01 Functions & Transformations","answer":"$x=\\frac{\\log10}{\\log2}\\approx\\frac{1}{0.301}\\approx3.322$.","explanation":"$x=\\frac{\\log10}{\\log2}\\approx\\frac{1}{0.301}\\approx3.322$."},{"q":"Solve $3^{2x}=50$ for $x$, rounded to three decimal places.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving exponential equations using logarithms","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences & Series","answer":"$2x=\\frac{\\log50}{\\log3}\\approx\\frac{1.699}{0.477}\\approx3.561$, so $x\\approx1.781$.","explanation":"$2x=\\frac{\\log50}{\\log3}\\approx\\frac{1.699}{0.477}\\approx3.561$, so $x\\approx1.781$."}]},{"heading":"Part IV — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Foundational Concept Mastery (21–28)","questions":[{"q":"The graph shows an exponential function. Based on the graph, does it represent growth or decay?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential growth and decay models","choices":["Neither","Growth","Cannot be determined","Decay"],"correct":1,"answer":"The curve rises as $x$ increases: growth.","explanation":"The curve rises as $x$ increases: growth.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2**x"],"xmin":-2,"xmax":3,"ymin":0,"ymax":9,"width":230}},{"q":"Write $4\\log x-\\log y$ as a single logarithm.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Log laws: the power rule","choices":["$\\log\\left(\\frac{x^4}{y}\\right)$","$\\log(4x-y)$","$4\\log\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)$","$\\log\\left(\\frac{4x}{y}\\right)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$4\\log x=\\log(x^4)$; combined: $\\log\\left(\\frac{x^4}{y}\\right)$.","explanation":"$4\\log x=\\log(x^4)$; combined: $\\log\\left(\\frac{x^4}{y}\\right)$."},{"q":"Condense $\\frac{1}{2}\\log x+2\\log y$ into a single logarithm.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions","choices":["$\\log(x\\cdot y^2)$","$\\log\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{y^2}\\right)$","$\\log(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^2)$","$\\log(2\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y)$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\frac{1}{2}\\log x=\\log\\sqrt{x}$; combined: $\\log(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^2)$.","explanation":"$\\frac{1}{2}\\log x=\\log\\sqrt{x}$; combined: $\\log(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^2)$."},{"q":"Solve $4^x=\\frac{1}{16}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","choices":["$x=4$","$x=-4$","$x=-2$","$x=2$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4^x=4^{-2}\\Rightarrow x=-2$.","explanation":"$4^x=4^{-2}\\Rightarrow x=-2$."},{"q":"Solve $2^{2x-1}=32$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Solving exponential equations (matching bases)","choices":["$x=3$","$x=2.5$","$x=6$","$x=5.5$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$2^{2x-1}=2^5\\Rightarrow2x-1=5\\Rightarrow x=3$.","explanation":"$2^{2x-1}=2^5\\Rightarrow2x-1=5\\Rightarrow x=3$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{e}\\right)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Natural logarithms and e","choices":["$1$","$e$","$-1$","$0$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\ln(e^{-1})=-1$.","explanation":"$\\ln(e^{-1})=-1$."},{"q":"Evaluate $e^{\\ln7}$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Natural logarithms and e","choices":["$7$","$\\ln7$","$1$","$e^7$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$e^{\\ln x}=x$.","explanation":"$e^{\\ln x}=x$."},{"q":"The population of a town is modeled by $P(t)=8{,}000e^{0.025t}$, where $t$ is in years. Find $P(15)$, rounded to the nearest whole number.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential growth and decay models","choices":["$8{,}300$","$11{,}000$","$11{,}640$","$12{,}000$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$P(15)=8{,}000e^{0.375}\\approx11{,}640$.","explanation":"$P(15)=8{,}000e^{0.375}\\approx11{,}640$."}]},{"heading":"Part V — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Intermediate Exam Application (29–37)","questions":[{"q":"Determine whether $N(t)=80e^{-0.015t}$ models growth or decay.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential growth and decay models","choices":["Decay","Neither","Growth","Cannot be determined"],"correct":0,"answer":"The exponent's coefficient is negative: decay.","explanation":"The exponent's coefficient is negative: decay."},{"q":"Determine whether $M(t)=30e^{0.01t}$ models growth or decay.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponential growth and decay models","choices":["Neither","Cannot be determined","Decay","Growth"],"correct":3,"answer":"The exponent's coefficient is positive: growth.","explanation":"The exponent's coefficient is positive: growth."},{"q":"An investment of 3,000 dollars grows according to $A(t)=3{,}000e^{0.05t}$ dollars, where $t$ is in years. Find the investment's value after 8 years, rounded to the nearest dollar.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems: exponential models in context","choices":["$4{,}200$","$4{,}800$","$4{,}475$","$3{,}400$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$A(8)=3{,}000e^{0.4}\\approx4{,}475$ dollars.","explanation":"$A(8)=3{,}000e^{0.4}\\approx4{,}475$ dollars."},{"q":"A cup of coffee cools according to $T(t)=22+70e^{-0.08t}$ (°C), where $t$ is in minutes. Find the temperature after 15 minutes, rounded to one decimal place.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems: exponential models in context","choices":["$38.5^\\circ$C","$50.0^\\circ$C","$43.1^\\circ$C","$22.0^\\circ$C"],"correct":2,"answer":"$T(15)=22+70e^{-1.2}\\approx43.1^\\circ$C.","explanation":"$T(15)=22+70e^{-1.2}\\approx43.1^\\circ$C."},{"q":"A population of bacteria doubles every 3 hours, starting at 500. Using $P(t)=500\\cdot2^{t/3}$, find the population after 9 hours.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems: exponential models in context","choices":["$4{,}000$","$2{,}000$","$8{,}000$","$1{,}500$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$P(9)=500\\times2^3=4{,}000$.","explanation":"$P(9)=500\\times2^3=4{,}000$."},{"q":"The value of a car depreciates according to $V(t)=25{,}000(0.85)^t$ dollars, where $t$ is in years. Find the car's value after 5 years, rounded to the nearest dollar.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Word problems: exponential models in context","choices":["$11{,}093$","$12{,}750$","$9{,}500$","$10{,}625$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$V(5)=25{,}000(0.85)^5\\approx11{,}093$ dollars.","explanation":"$V(5)=25{,}000(0.85)^5\\approx11{,}093$ dollars."},{"q":"Evaluate $4^{\\frac{1}{2}}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$4$","$5$","$2$","$6$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4^{\\frac{1}{2}}=2$.","explanation":"$4^{\\frac{1}{2}}=2$."},{"q":"In a laboratory calibration sequence, evaluate $5^{2}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$27$","$10$","$23$","$25$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$5^{2}=25$.","explanation":"$5^{2}=25$."},{"q":"Solve $4^{x}=256$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$4$","$3$","$6$","$5$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$256=4^{4}$, so $x=4$.","explanation":"$256=4^{4}$, so $x=4$."}]},{"heading":"Part VI — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (38–45)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $4^{x-3}=16$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$5$","$6$","$2$","$4$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$16=4^{2}$, so $x-3=2\\Rightarrow x=5$.","explanation":"$16=4^{2}$, so $x-3=2\\Rightarrow x=5$.","cross_lesson":"1.01 Algebra & Equations"},{"q":"Combine $\\log_{2} 2+\\log_{2} 2$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$3$","$1$","$4$","$2$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\log_{2}(2\\times2)=\\log_{2} 4=2$ (since $2^{2}=4$).","explanation":"$\\log_{2}(2\\times2)=\\log_{2} 4=2$ (since $2^{2}=4$).","cross_lesson":"2.01 Functions & Transformations"},{"q":"Combine $\\log_{5} 125-\\log_{5} 25$ into a single logarithm and evaluate.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$3$","$5$","$1$","$2$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{125}{25}\\right)=\\log_{5} 5=1$.","explanation":"$\\log_{5}\\left(\\frac{125}{25}\\right)=\\log_{5} 5=1$.","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences & Series"},{"q":"Evaluate $\\log_{2}(8^{2})$ using the power rule.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$6$","$8$","$5$","$4$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\log_{2}(8^{2})=2\\log_{2} 8=2(3)=6$.","explanation":"$\\log_{2}(8^{2})=2\\log_{2} 8=2(3)=6$.","cross_lesson":"4.01 Trigonometry"},{"q":"Solve $\\log_{5}(x-2)=4$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$629$","$630$","$627$","$625$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$x-2=5^{4}=625\\Rightarrow x=627$.","explanation":"$x-2=5^{4}=625\\Rightarrow x=627$.","cross_lesson":"5.01 Geometry & Coordinate Geometry"},{"q":"Solve $\\log_{5}(x)=3$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$123$","$128$","$125$","$127$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$x=5^{3}=125$.","explanation":"$x=5^{3}=125$.","cross_lesson":"6.01 Limits & Derivatives"},{"q":"Evaluate $\\ln(e^{6})$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$5$","$7$","$6$","$e^{6}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\ln(e^{6})=6$.","explanation":"$\\ln(e^{6})=6$.","cross_lesson":"7.01 Integration & Applications"},{"q":"A quantity is modeled by $N(t)=500e^{-0.1t}$. Find $N(5)$, rounded to one decimal place.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Exponentials & Logarithms","choices":["$273.0$","$500$","$303.3$","$333.6$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$N(5)=500e^{-0.5}=500(0.60653)\\approx303.3$.","explanation":"$N(5)=500e^{-0.5}=500(0.60653)\\approx303.3$.","cross_lesson":"9.01 Statistics & Probability"}]}]}